-- title:
--   Soundness of the compact critical-line sign check
-- statement:
--   Let $d$ be compact critical-line sample data, with claimed sign bit $b$ and height
--   $t$. Let $g(t)$ be the real completed-zeta line function used by the certificate.
--   If the point checker succeeds, then
--   $$b=\mathrm{true}\Rightarrow g(t)>0,\qquad
--   b=\mathrm{false}\Rightarrow g(t)<0.$$
--   Thus a successful arithmetic check certifies the sign asserted by the sample.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/Arb4_Line.lean#L115-L147

